  "published": "2026-01-17T17:52:26.08Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "🎉 Initial Release v1.0.0\n      \n      ✨ Features:\n      • Distributed circuit breaker with Redis state coordination\n      • All instances share circuit state - when one breaks, all stop\n      • Distributed locking prevents race conditions\n      • Simple fluent API: CircuitBreaker.Create(\"id\", \"redis\")\n      • Automatic fallback to in-memory if Redis unavailable\n      • Works with ALL Redis providers (Azure, AWS, Redis Cloud, self-hosted)\n      • Built-in resilience patterns\n      \n      🔧 Technical:\n      • Based on Polly 8.5.0 concepts\n      • Redis SETNX for distributed locking\n      • Lua scripts for atomic operations\n      • State machine pattern implementation\n      \n      📚 Perfect for:\n      • Microservices architectures\n      • Kubernetes/Docker deployments\n      • Cloud-native applications\n      • Scaled systems with multiple instances",
  "repository": "",
  "title": "Distributed Circuit Breaker for .NET using Redis",
